msg_instruction_01_en="How MikroTik Backup Script works"
msg_instruction_02_en="Purpose:"
msg_instruction_03_en="This script creates RouterOS backups."
msg_instruction_04_en="It can operate in two main modes:"
msg_instruction_05_en="- with one device through the interactive Master or command line;"
msg_instruction_06_en="- with several devices in batch mode."
msg_instruction_07_en="Depending on the settings, two kinds of backups can be created:"
msg_instruction_08_en="- RouterOS configuration in an .rsc file;"
msg_instruction_09_en="- Binary backup in a .backup file;"
msg_instruction_10_en="Script settings"
msg_instruction_11_en="All parameters required by the script are built into it."
msg_instruction_12_en="Some are optional and can be changed using option.cfg in the same directory as the script."
msg_instruction_13_en="It can define the backup directory, device-list source, backup types, monthly archiving, incrementality and other common parameters."
msg_instruction_14_en="option.cfg can be created manually or with the editor started by this key:"
msg_instruction_15_en="./mikrotik-backup.sh -e"
msg_instruction_16_en="Command-line mode"
msg_instruction_17_en="At minimum, only three parameters are required: IP address, login and password."
msg_instruction_18_en="./mikrotik-backup.sh -a=xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx -u=user -p=password"
msg_instruction_19_en="The remaining command-line parameters are optional."
msg_instruction_20_en="Display their reference with:"
msg_instruction_21_en="./mikrotik-backup.sh -h"
msg_instruction_22_en="Batch mode"
msg_instruction_23_en="This mode requires devicelist.cfg in the same directory as the script. List device names and connection data in that file."
msg_instruction_24_en="Create the file manually or use BackUP Master."
msg_instruction_25_en="Where to find backups"
msg_instruction_26_en="The storage directory is set by BackupRoot in option.cfg."
msg_instruction_27_en="If BackupRoot is absent, or option.cfg has not been created, device backups are placed in the backups directory next to mikrotik-backup.sh."
msg_instruction_28_en="If BackupRoot points to network storage, set UseNetFolder=true. This enables availability checks before backups are created."
